  "consentTitle": "Your data, your rights",
  "@consentTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in help tips (core), and 2 other places."
  },
  "consentIntro": "Before you use DesKilo, here is what the app does with your data, who can see it and what you can do about it. Two minutes; it is all there is.",
  "@consentIntro": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in consent screen (profile)."
  },
  "consentWhatTitle": "What DesKilo processes",
  "@consentWhatTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentWhatBody": "Your account (e-mail, display name, hashed password), your profile as you fill it (photo, status, address, WhatsApp number — each optional), and what you do in a space: bookings and check-ins, messages, expenses and consumptions, your subscription, invoices and payments. All of it is stored on the server your space runs on: on the shared reference server, in the EU (Supabase, eu-central-1); on a server a community runs itself, wherever its operator chose. Settings → Privacy & data shows that server's notice: who runs it, where the data is and who receives it.",
  "@consentWhatBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentNotTitle": "What DesKilo never does",
  "@consentNotTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentNotBody": "No tracking, no analytics, no advertising, no sale of data. Your data goes to nobody except the recipients named here and in the server's notice. The F-Droid build has no Google services at all.",
  "@consentNotBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentWhoTitle": "Who can see what",
  "@consentWhoTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentWhoBody": "Access follows roles and is enforced on the server: bookings are visible to the space (the floor plan shows occupancy); your finances and your commercial agreement only to you, the owners and the admins holding the matching permission. Each item of your profile is shown only to the audience you pick under Who sees me; nothing is public unless you choose it.",
  "@consentWhoBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentWhoBodyPublic": "A public profile stays off until you publish it: then anyone with the link reads your name, profession and bio — never your contact details, presence or spaces — until you withdraw it. Settings → Privacy & data names the people and lists who actually looked.",
  "@consentWhoBodyPublic": {
    "description": "#3485 The second half of the consent text on who sees what: the public profile (kept apart so no message passes 600 characters)."
  },
  "consentMessagesBody": "Only the people in a conversation can open it: the two of you, the members of a group or, when you write to a space, the hosts the app names before you send. A space's owners and admins cannot read your conversations. Messages are not end-to-end encrypted: they are stored on the server the conversation lives on — another server's, after you confirm, when you write to someone there — and whoever runs that server can technically reach them.",
  "@consentMessagesBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentPushTitle": "Push notifications",
  "@consentPushTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentPushBody": "Optional, and outbound. When the server's operator has set push up, your space uses it and it is on for this device, this device's address and each notification go to the push service (Firebase Cloud Messaging, which hands notifications for Apple devices on to Apple). A notification only says something generic, such as \"You have a new message\": no names, no times, no message text. Switch it off in Settings → Privacy & data; the app keeps working and nothing more is sent to this device.",
  "@consentPushBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentControllerTitle": "Who is responsible",
  "@consentControllerTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentControllerBody": "Each space is run by its owner — your community — who decides members, prices and payment providers. Each server is run by its operator: the shared reference server by Florian Dittgen (Germany), a community's own server by whoever runs it. The app is free software (AGPL-3.0-or-later), published by Florian Dittgen. Online payments go through the provider the owner enabled (PayPal, Stripe, Mollie, Wero) under that provider's terms.",
  "@consentControllerBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentRetentionTitle": "How long",
  "@consentRetentionTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentRetentionBody": "As long as you are a member. When you leave a space and erase, your messages in that space go, and your profile goes with your last space. Accounting records stay for the legal retention period: the ledger by identifier, invoices as they were issued.",
  "@consentRetentionBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentRightsTitle": "Your rights",
  "@consentRightsTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentRightsBody": "Access, rectification, export (art. 20), erasure (art. 17) and objection — each is a button in Settings → Privacy & data. For anything else: fdittgen@gmail.com. You may withdraw this consent by leaving the workspace and erasing your data at any time.",
  "@consentRightsBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentReviewTitle": "Read it again anytime",
  "@consentReviewTitle": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
  "consentReviewBody": "This text stays available in Settings → Privacy & data, in the in-app help (Privacy) and in the online user guide. A change of the text asks for your acceptance again.",
  "@consentReviewBody": {
    "description": "Shown as the text in privacy policy (core)."
  },
